# Trivy suppressions.
#
# One CVE per line. Every entry must carry a reason and a review date, because a suppression with
# neither is indistinguishable from an oversight and outlives whoever added it:
#
#   # CVE-2024-12345 -- transitive via foo:bar, not reachable: we never call the affected codec.
#   # Review by 2026-12-01, or when foo:bar 2.x lands.
#   CVE-2024-12345
#
# The scan blocks on CRITICAL only. HIGH findings appear in the Security tab rather than failing
# the build, so they do not need suppressing here to keep CI green; suppress a HIGH only if the
# noise is actively obscuring something.

# CVE-2026-47884 -- spring-webmvc 6.2.19, XsltView SSRF/RCE via a "/**" mapping with an implicit
# view name. Not reachable: the vault is a JSON REST API with no ViewResolver and no XsltView
# (grep over src finds neither). The 6.2.20 fix is Enterprise-only; the open-source fix is
# Spring Framework 7.0.9, i.e. the Spring Boot 4 migration tracked separately.
# Review by 2027-02-28, or when the Boot 4 migration lands, whichever is first.
CVE-2026-47884

# CVE-2026-47890 -- spring-webmvc 6.2.19, Server-Sent Event stream corruption while rendering
# fragments. Not reachable: the vault serves no SSE and renders no view fragments. Same fix path
# and review date as CVE-2026-47884.
CVE-2026-47890
